Settings: a AGC; m Mic Gain; p Power; s Step Size; t Tuner; v VFO/receiver; e Speech Processor. q returns and announces Back, or Done after AGC selection. h reads this help.

s a reads the current AGC setting without changing it. Another a selects the next AGC setting and announces the confirmed choice. q finishes and announces Done. Fast recovers sooner after a strong signal; Slow holds gain reduction longer. Choose by listening. Off allows larger changes in received volume. No transmission is needed.

m opens guided microphone adjustment. Follow the preparation prompts; h inside explains the test, keys and ALC feedback. You operate PTT yourself.

p announces current power and the entry range. Type whole watts and press Enter; blank Enter cancels. A confirmed change announces the entered value followed by Set. This is a setting, not measured transmitted power. h then Enter gives power help. Blank Enter or q then Enter cancels and returns to Settings.

s opens tuning step entry for the current mode. t cycles tuner choices and announces the confirmed setting; it does not start tuning. Leave Settings and press t to start a tuning cycle. v selects the supported VFO or receiver and reports the selection.

e opens Speech Processor and reads its settings. e inside toggles it; full stop increases and comma decreases the selected level. n cancels and restores entry processor settings; q keeps changes. h inside explains the available controls and feedback.

Model-specific choices, limits and exceptions are in doc/supported-radios: open the text file named for your radio. READ-ME.txt explains these notes. Spoken responses are also written as text for the braille display. Unsupported controls and failed or unknown readings are reported.


s b: full stop or b selects the next mode; comma the previous. q applies, saves and returns. h reads help. Braille only silences Speakup; connected braille remains available in every mode.

s o: r Rate; v Volume; p Pitch; u Punctuation; full stop increases; comma decreases; t Test; d Defaults; h Help; q returns. Changes apply and save immediately.

s u: Update YAC. Shows help, then Looking. No Internet or No Update returns to Settings. Update Found asks Read Notes Y/N?, then Update Y/N?. y accepts; n skips notes or declines installation; q returns. Long notes use Space for the next page and q to leave.

s w: Wi-Fi setup is available only on the Raspberry Pi image. Use your operating system Wi-Fi settings here. Wi-Fi setup. Country, network name and password. Ctrl+C cancels entry; punctuation and command letters are literal.

